-- title:
--   Igusa charts inside Gauss reductions of σ-twisted j-charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $M\neq 0$, $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137), i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of that rational function field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; let $j\in K$ have $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), with $j\neq 0$ assumed as an instance. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra, and $w$ an [`ModularCurve.IntegralWeightOneForm k M`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L16), that is a weight one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion whose associated series over $k$ is nonzero. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ such that: the $q$-expansion of $\sigma j$ is [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) read in $L((q))$ (substitution $q\mapsto q^p$ in $j$); $\sigma$ preserves the subalgebra [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), namely `chartAlg A ↥K {j}`, in the sense that $b$ lies in it iff $\sigma b$ does; and, for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ whose elements are exactly those $f$ admitting a presentation $f\cdot y=x$ in $L((q))$ with $x,y\in A[[q]]$ and $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, the comap of $W_0$ along $\sigma$ is different from $W_0$ and contains both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every $P\in A[X]$ with nonzero reduction. Finally let $t$ be an element of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) $\subseteq k((q))$ with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15). The conclusion is the conjunction of two inclusions of sets of Laurent series over $k$: every $z$ in the Igusa function field integral over $k[t]$ (the chart ring [`AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.chartRing k {t}`](def/JacJ1_ChartAlgebra.html#L45)) has its $q$-expansion in the $k$-subalgebra of $k((q))$ generated by all $r=\bar x/\bar y$ arising from some $b\in$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` and $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal and $\sigma(b)\cdot y=x$ in $L((q))$, the bars denoting images under $A\to k$; and likewise every $z$ integral over $k[t^{-1}]$ has its $q$-expansion in the corresponding $k$-subalgebra built from [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144), that is `chartAlg A ↥K {j⁻¹}`.
--
--   This is the set-theoretic core of the normality statement for the second component of the special fibre of the model of $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_1(p))$ over a discrete valuation ring with residue characteristic $p$: read through the level-$p$ involution $\sigma$, the two affine rings of the Igusa curve in characteristic $p$ are generated by Gauss reductions of the integral $j$-charts. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_surjective_tensorProduct_chartAlg_to_chartRing_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_of_algEquiv_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_surjective_tensorProduct_chartAlg_to_chartRing_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_of_algEquiv_x1_mul), the surjectivity assertion from which normality of that component is deduced.
